{"name":"Black Spruce","hex":"#4c5752","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black spruce","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Picea mariana, a North American species of spruce."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_spruce"}],"entries":[{"title":"Picea mariana","blocks":[{"text":"Picea mariana, the black spruce, is a North American species of spruce tree in the pine family. It is widespread across Canada, found in all 10 provinces and all 3 territories. It is the official tree of Newfoundland and Labrador and is that province's most abundant tree. Its range extends into northern parts of the United States: in Alaska, the Great Lakes region, and the upper Northeast. It is a frequent part of the biome known as taiga or boreal forest."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Black_spruce_stand_at_Arctic_Chalet%2C_Inuvik%2C_NT.jpg/330px-Black_spruce_stand_at_Arctic_Chalet%2C_Inuvik%2C_NT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picea_mariana"},{"title":"Spruce","blocks":[{"text":"A spruce is a tree of the genus Picea, a genus of some 37 species of coniferous trees in the pine family, Pinaceae, found in the northern temperate and boreal (taiga) regions of the Northern Hemisphere. Picea is treated either in the subfamily Pinoideae, or the sole genus in its own subfamily Piceoideae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Picea_abies.jpg/330px-Picea_abies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spruce"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Picea_mariana_levila.png/500px-Picea_mariana_levila.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Picea_mariana_levila.png/500px-Picea_mariana_levila.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APicea_mariana_levila.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Picea_mariana_cones.jpg/500px-Picea_mariana_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Picea_mariana_cones.jpg/1280px-Picea_mariana_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Picea_mariana_cones.jpg/500px-Picea_mariana_cones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Needles and young cones","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APicea_mariana_cones.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Picea_mariana_taiga.jpg/500px-Picea_mariana_taiga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Picea_mariana_taiga.jpg/500px-Picea_mariana_taiga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig